<grade verdict="partial" score="0.5">The binary is right: "B is 1011 and 7 is 0111". The decimal goes wrong at "B is 12": the letter digits run A = 10, B = 11, C = 12, so it is 11 × 16 + 7 = 183.</grade>

<card>What are the decimal values of the hex digits A to F? :: A = 10, B = 11, C = 12, D = 13, E = 14, F = 15.</card>

<note>Hex digits: A = 10, B = 11, C = 12, D = 13, E = 14, F = 15. A two-digit hex number with digits h and l is 16 × h + l.</note>

**Problem 2 · a little harder**

Convert decimal 300 to hexadecimal.

<solution>300 = 1 × 256 + 44; 44 = 2 × 16 + 12; 12 is C. So 0x12C.</solution>
