<summary>**What came back:** splitting a hex number into 4-bit groups, and converting decimal to hex by repeated division (300 = 0x12C).

**Still shaky:** the values of the letter digits. You took B as 12 in the first problem, then had C = 12 right in the second; the card for A to F is in your deck.

